Why the whole tarball and not a subset
--------------------------------------
Every other vendored corpus in these repos is a trimmed subset.  This one is
not, and the reason is the licence rather than convenience.  The largest
collection inside it is James Clark's "XML Test Cases version 1998-11-18"
(xmlconf/xmltest/), whose own readme.html says:

    Copyright (C) 1998 James Clark.  All rights reserved.  Permission is
    granted to copy and modify this collection in any way for internal use
    within a company or organization.  Permission is granted to
    redistribute the file xmltest.zip containing this collection to third
    parties provided that no modifications of any kind are made to this
    file.  Note that permission to distribute the collection in any other
    form is not granted.

Redistribution is permitted only for the unmodified archive.  The W3C tarball
is the archive the W3C itself redistributes, so vendoring it verbatim is the
form that stays inside that grant; a hand-picked subset would not.

t/suite.py selects the subset it scores at run time, from xmlconf.xml, and
never rewrites a test file.

